# Fleeing a travel encounter that fired on the journey's LAST step leaves the party where it came from.
#
# The encounter on the last step stands between the party and the destination: the step has been
# taken, and the arrival announced and held, when the fight opens. A party that runs has not reached
# the place. It used to be left standing on it all the same — unentered, and unenterable, because the
# map refuses a journey to the vertex underfoot ("you have been there — choose somewhere else"). It
# now falls back to the cell the step left from, which for a one-cell journey is where it set out.
#
# --encounter-on-arrival stages that step, as in fight_victory_travel_arrival.cli, which is the
# victory half of the same case.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --encounter-on-arrival wolf

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60

# One cell, so the step the encounter interrupts is also the first: the origin is the cell it left.
travel neighbour
travel-go

wait mode EncounterPrompt 90
click engage
wait mode Fighting 90
# A journey thins the music to one track; the fight it runs into plays the whole band.
expect-state music tracks=4 filter=Fighting

fight-end runaway
wait mode WorldView 90

inspect avatar
expect-state avatar on=origin
expect-no-state avatar on=destination
quit
